# No Git Operations

Do not run any git commands or git-related processes in this project unless the user explicitly asks for a specific git operation in that message.

## Forbidden

- `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, `git pull`, `git fetch`
- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log`, `git branch`, `git checkout`, `git merge`, `git rebase`
- Creating commits, branches, tags, or pull requests
- Any other git workflow step, including read-only inspection

## Required behavior

- Make file changes directly; do not stage or commit them.
- If git would normally help (status, diff, history), use non-git tools instead (Read, Grep, Glob).
- If the user asks to save work, edit files only — do not commit or push.
- If git is needed, ask the user to run the commands themselves unless they explicitly request a specific git command.
